Links are data in a file people edit, and cycles also arise without
editing: a deck that asks the same question twice links its first
occurrence's successor back to it.  The walk must end on a cycle, a link
to a question the store does not hold, and a link that is not a hash at
all.  A serial that is missing from a linked question cannot be checked,
so the store is read by the serial rule, which takes the question's
position instead.  A repeated question is live at its last position only; its
earlier neighbours fall out of the sequence, which is the price of one
entry per hash and was the same under the serials.

