An older Mentipy that builds into a store with links copies every link
unchanged and gives each question it registers the next value of its
counter.  The helper below does to the file exactly that, as 0.16's
[[register]] did: pop each question, give it a serial one above the
largest in the store, re-append it with its other keys, the stale link
included, and add a question it has not seen without a link.  The live
sequence must then be what that older version shows itself, never a
question its build dropped.  Each check is needed on its own.  Adding a
question in front leaves a chain whose steps all agree but whose head,
re-registered by the older build, has a serial above one; reordering
leaves a head with serial~1 that the older build did not touch and a
stale step to it.

<<test functions>>=
def _as_rebuilt_by_0_16(path, texts):
    data = json.loads(path.read_text())
    questions = data["questions"]
    serial = max(meta[REGISTRATION_SERIAL_KEY] for meta in questions.values())
    for text in texts:
        question = OpenQuestion(text)
        full_hash = question_hash(question)
        entry = questions.pop(full_hash, None)
        if entry is None:
            entry = {**question.to_dict(), "url_prefix": full_hash[:8]}
            data["answers"][full_hash] = []
        serial += 1
        entry[REGISTRATION_SERIAL_KEY] = serial
        questions[full_hash] = entry
    data["registration_counter"] = serial
    path.write_text(json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + "\n")


