Stores written by older versions hold absolute paths under the legacy
key.  We fake one by writing the JSON the way the old code wrote it.
Any write of the store migrates every question's legacy list, here a
plain registration of an unrelated question.  The entries of this
checkout whose directory exists move to [[qr_paths]], relative and
merged with what is already there; everything else is dropped: an
entry whose directory has gone, a nested worktree's file, a sibling
worktree's, another platform's path, and a non-string.  The legacy key
is gone afterwards.

