@

A ranking aggregates into mean ranks rather than counts.  Two respondents
who swap the top two options leave those options tied on a mean rank of
[[1.5]] while the unanimously last option keeps its rank of [[3]], and the
best-first [[order]] breaks the tie by option index.

<<test functions>>=

